significantly'","why":"Deferred borrowing must eventually be taken in a market where the 10-year PWLB certainty rate ended the year at 5.72%, up from 5.38%."},{"code":"borrowing-increase","headline":"Borrowing rose \u00a334.696m to \u00a3443.572m in 2025/26 (\u00a357m new PWLB at 4.663% average), and the liability benchmark shows the net loans requirement doubling from \u00a3351.572m to \u00a3703.839m by 31 March 2027 and \u00a3812.405m by 31 March 2028","why":"Existing borrowing is forecast at only \u00a3434.601m by March 2027, so the benchmark implies roughly \u00a3270m of new external borrowing within two years to fund the capital programme."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"cfr","value":"\u00a3964.792m total CFR (GF \u00a3212.176m, HRA \u00a3656.364m, IFRS16 leases \u00a328.879m, PFI \u00a372.609m at 31.3.25 basis shown as \u00a367.373m at 31.3.26); borrowing CFR \u00a3868.540m","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":3},{"name":"borrowing","value":"\u00a3443.572m total borrowing at 4.401% average (PWLB \u00a3442.572m at 4.408%, green bond \u00a31.000m at 1.550%), up \u00a334.696m from \u00a3408.876m; no LOBOs, no short-term borrowing","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":4},{"name":"new borrowing","value":"\u00a357.000m of new PWLB maturity loans in year at 4.663% average rate, 7.439 years average period","page":7},{"name":"internal borrowing","value":"\u00a3424.968m (borrowing CFR \u00a3868.540m vs external borrowing \u00a3443.572m), up from \u00a3402.008m at 31.3.25","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":3},{"name":"total investments","value":"\u00a392.000m at 4.350% average income return (government \u00a319m, local authorities and other govt entities \u00a333m, money market funds \u00a340m); balances ranged \u00a379m-\u00a3115m during the year","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":8},{"name":"la lending","value":"\u00a333.000m placed with local authorities and other government entities (income return 5.379%, WAM 54.394 days)","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":8},{"name":"la borrowing short term","value":"\u00a30.000m \u2014 the Council had no short-term loans as at 31st March 2026","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":7},{"name":"investment income","value":"\u00a35.1m investment income earned vs \u00a31.75m budget, due to higher-for-longer rates and larger than expected cash balances","page":8},{"name":"treasury outturn vs budget","value":"external borrowing \u00a357m taken vs \u00a3162.216m forecast (HRA \u00a3127.374m forecast/\u00a357m taken; GF \u00a334.842m forecast/none taken); treasury investments \u00a392m vs \u00a330m forecast","page":11},{"name":"total debt","value":"\u00a3539.824m total debt including \u00a396.252m PFI and leases, vs \u00a31,033.968m operational boundary and \u00a31,085.667m authorised limit; remaining borrowing capacity \u00a3545.843m","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":12},{"name":"liability benchmark","value":"net loans requirement \u00a3351.572m actual at 31.3.26, forecast \u00a3703.839m at 31.3.27 and \u00a3812.405m at 31.3.28, vs existing borrowing of \u00a3434.601m and \u00a3430.965m respectively","page":12},{"name":"maturity under 12m","value":"2% of borrowing under 12 months (maturity structure table, actual column headed 31.3.25; \u00a38.668m of HRA loans mature in the period per para 4.14)","page":13},{"name":"commercial portfolio","value":"\u00a327.535m held in directly owned investment property (Statement of Accounts value as at 31.03.2026), generating \u00a32.342m net investment income in 2025/26, a 4.25% rate of return","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":10}],"commercial":{"commercial_portfolio":{"value":"\u00a327.535m held in directly owned investment property (Statement of Accounts value as at 31.03.2026), generating \u00a32.342m net investment income in 2025/26, a 4.25% rate of return","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":10,"doc":"Treasury Management Outturn - 1033284"}},"tms_components":null},"compliance":null,"documents":[{"title":"Committee report Treasury Full Year 2026 LIs","url":"https://islington.moderngov.co.uk/documents